smartinit.v3.3.2  Q1FY15 
February 2015 NAM/DGEX smartinit upgrade to coincide with RTMA/URMA upgrade

- Synchronized NAM and GFS smartinit systems
- Correction to 2m temperature hour minus 1 and hour minus 2 labels in 3 hourly DNG files
- Addition of Haines Index Fire weather product to NAM and DGEX CONUS and Alaska DNG grids
  for transmittal through AWIPS

===================================================================================
1.  Synchronized NAM/DGEX and GFS smartinit systems

*   The v3.3.2 system includes all changes needed to run downscaling from NAM, DGEX or GFS parent models
The same executables, smartinit and smartprecip can be used for either parent model.
Different jobs/scripts/ush codes are provided for each parent model.  
Currently NAM and DGEX DNG take advantage of this synchronization.  GFS DNG will be upgraded for a future
implementation of GFS

2.  Correction of 2m Temperature hour minus 1 and hour minus 2 labels in 3 hourly DNG files

* Fixed the mislabelling of the NAM/DGEX off-hour 2-m temperature records in the 3-hourly DNG files; 
for example, in the 3-h NAM DNG file, 2-m T at hour 1 was labelled as hour 2, and hour 2 was labelled as hour 1.
These now will be labelled correctly.  These fields are only available on ftpprd.


3. Addition of Haines Index Fire weather product to NAM and DGEX CONUS and Alaska DNG grids
  for transmittal through AWIPS.

* NCO modified the current NAM WMO header data cards and created new DGEX WMO header data cards
to include Haines Index (Fire Weather) downscaled fields to AWIPS grib2 files for CONUS and Alaska
DNG grids.  More information is found at the NCO provided documentation:
https://docs.google.com/a/noaa.gov/document/d/1i8Tmwot9WPgGUNqdKSnO4JhjDZF4jX-fkuAri_Qk_qc/edit

#===============================================================================
 IMPLEMENTATION INSTRUCTIONS 
#===============================================================================
1. svn checkout https://svnemc.ncep.noaa.gov/projects/smartinit/tags/RB-V3.3.2


2.  Build sorc codes smartinit.fd, smartprecip.fd
        cd smartinit.${model_ver}/sorc/smartinit.fd
        make
          This will create smartinit  executable in ../../smartinit.${model_ver}/exec
        cd ...smartinit.${model_ver}/sorc/smartprecip.fd
        make
          This will create smartprecip  executable in ../../smartinit.${model_ver}/exec

3.  Use ...docs/smartinit.ver file if desired to set
      model_ver=v3.3.2  parameter

4.  See ...docs/bjobcards-dev for recommended limits to use in JNAM_SMINIT jobs.
    eg:
#BSUB -W 03:00
#BSUB -n 1
#BSUB -R affinity[core]
#BSUB -R rusage[mem=5500]
#BSUB -q dev

5.  RUNTYP,cyc, ffhr are specified in ecflow scripts provided in smartinit.${model_ver}/ecf directory


NOTE: Details on all changes to nam smartinit are found at /meso/save/Jeff.McQueen/smartrun/docs/README

